# Source findings: complete editorial review

Every existing finding is classified individually. Authored content, source flags, inferred relationships and all repetitions remain unchanged. Import approval is false. Recommendations and thematic candidate verses are not author decisions.

Review status: AUTHOR_FINDINGS_REVIEWED. This describes author decisions on findings, not canonical-content or import approval. Accepted preservation retains the original uncertainty.

Decisions: pending 0; accepted 206; correction_requested 0; deferred 0. Author identity: author.

| Classification | Findings | Author decisions | Review guidance |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| source_omission | 31 | 31 accepted | Supply exact authored wording, or explicitly accept this reference as unresolved; separately decide its probable note anchor. |
| unconfirmed_relationship | 31 | 31 accepted | Confirm or replace the probable anchor. Author confirmation does not create a footnote marker in the original PDF. |
| broken_citation | 3 | 3 accepted | Specify the intended existing reference, or accept the original broken citation with its unresolved status. |
| source_attested_repetition | 67 | 67 accepted | Confirm intentional repetition, request specific revisions, or defer. Preserve every occurrence meanwhile. |
| legacy_citation | 24 | 24 accepted | Decide whether to preserve the historical citation or specify exact title/address changes. Do not assume renumbering from a title change. |
| printed_punctuation | 1 | 1 accepted | Accept the printed punctuation/styles or specify exact changes for individual examples. |
| uncertain_spacing | 49 | 49 accepted | Confirm the displayed dash join or specify exact spacing. PDF line wrapping cannot establish intended spaces. |

Decisions live in [AUTHOR_DECISIONS.json](AUTHOR_DECISIONS.json), separately from regenerable evidence. Each decision is bound to its finding fingerprint and all ten data-file hashes. Pending/deferred/correction-requested cases remain open; acceptance does not approve an import or rewrite a source.

The author identified themselves in this conversation. No substantive editorial decision has been inferred from that identity statement or from a question about passage groups.

