stream
# Deploy the frontend to Vercel

The React/Vite frontend deploys as a static site. The backend remains a separate
service. Deploying the frontend does not start Express, connect a database, or
enable accounts/community features by itself.

## Import the repository

Commit and push the reviewed frontend configuration before importing
`GreatRoyce/The-Human-Testament` into Vercel. Use these project settings:

| Setting | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Framework Preset | Vite |
| Root Directory | `frontend` |
| Include files outside the root directory in the Build Step | Enabled |
| Install Command | `npm ci && npm ci --prefix ../backend --omit=dev` |
| Build Command | `npm run build` |
| Output Directory | `dist` |
| Node.js Version | `22.x` (latest patched version provided by Vercel) |

The commands and output directory are also set in `frontend/vercel.json`.
The frontend imports `shared/manuscript.json`; its existing `prebuild` script
also uses backend dependencies and source files to verify the bundle against
the manuscript. Keep `backend/` and `shared/` available during the build.
Installing backend dependencies here supports verification; it does not deploy
the backend. Only `frontend/dist` is served.

## Public environment variables

Set these explicitly for both **Production** and **Preview** in Vercel:

| Variable | Frontend-only reader | With a hosted backend |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `VITE_CONTENT_SOURCE` | `pdf` | `pdf`, or `api` to load manuscript content from the backend |
| `VITE_API_URL` | Leave unset | Your HTTPS backend origin, for example `https://api.example.com` |
| `VITE_ANALYTICS_ENABLED` | `false` | `false` until backend analytics is configured |

Do not copy the local development API URL (`http://localhost:5000`). API URLs
must omit a trailing `/api`, credentials, query strings and fragments. API
content mode and enabled analytics require a backend URL. A frontend-only build
supports the bundled reader and search; account and community requests report
configuration errors until a backend is connected.

Disable **Automatically expose System Environment Variables** in Vercel's
Environment Variables settings. This project's production validator accepts
only the three `VITE_` variables above; extra framework-prefixed variables such
as `VITE_VERCEL_ENV` are rejected. Never put database, JWT or mail credentials
in frontend variables. Redeploy after changing build-time variables.

## Connect the backend later

Set `VITE_API_URL` to the deployed backend origin and redeploy the frontend.
Configure the backend's `AUTH_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` with the exact HTTPS frontend
origin. Set `PASSWORD_RESET_FRONTEND_URL` and
`EMAIL_VERIFICATION_FRONTEND_URL` to that same origin for emailed account links.
Preview origins need explicit authorization if they use account features.

Follow the existing [backend deployment runbook](../../backend/docs/DEPLOYMENT.md)
for backend setup and release checks. Frontend hosting does not resolve the
production findings recorded there.

## Verify the deployment

The SPA rewrite follows [Vercel's Vite guidance](https://vercel.com/docs/frameworks/frontend/vite#using-vite-to-make-spas),
excluding `/api`, `/assets` and paths ending in a file extension so missing
assets and accidental same-origin API requests retain their 404s.

After deploying, open and refresh `/`, `/testament/freedom/10/14`,
`/search?q=responsibility` and `/login` directly. Confirm reader/search content
loads, images and styles load, and a missing `/assets/missing.js` returns 404.
If a backend is configured, verify its health/readiness and real HTTPS account
flows separately. Local lint, tests, builds and server rendering do not prove
Vercel routing or browser behavior.

References: [build settings](https://vercel.com/docs/builds/configure-a-build),
[system environment variables](https://vercel.com/docs/environment-variables/system-environment-variables).

endstream
endobj
